      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Is this memory leak world instance bound or system bound or world system bound?\nIf it is world instance bound the memory usage would drop as soon as you swap to a new instance of the same world.\nIf it's system bound even changing to a different world would not change it and after restart this leak would occur in any world under same conditions.\nIf it's world system bound it would rapidly start using memory as soon as players join and start being active interacting in/with the world.\nFor example if the world has some kind of excessive memory allocation in it's design/udon-code.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
