      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "I have almost two identical laptops. The secondary one is kind of interesting as I'm using it as an idlebot in a public pug to offset the 'chair glitch' which has been happening in the last few months. In my findings i've noticed the client on the second laptop not only hasn't crashed in over 24 hours of the game being active, But it hasn't shown any sign of memory leak. \nI see no point having anything enabled on this account so under safety settings everything is off on that account. Including voices, even for friends. I believe that it's actually the avatars we use that may be potentially causing this memory leak issue. \nI can be in the same lobby as the second computer on my same network, almost identical specs, and I can't be in the lobby for more than two hours before I have to restart my client. My typical safety settings on my main is Friends = everything, All other ranks = Avatar, Voice, Icons.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
